[Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  i think the best types of relationships  between mentors and mentees are ones  where there's a really unique  fit between the two what do i mean by  that well i get a lot of requests  people asking for mentorship where they  want to know how do i succeed in data  science or how do i learn machine  learning or please mentor me give me  project ideas about  something really broad and i just think  there are  potentially many good mentors for this  person  but i'm not sure that i'm particularly  well suited to health when you're  looking for a mentor make sure you do  your due diligence by coming to the  table with research either about that  person  or about the technology that you'd like  some help on so check out the person on  linkedin  find out what their experience is or  maybe you want to  first look at a white paper or do some  research in that area  and come to the conversation with points  that you'd like their opinion on  so my advice for finding a mentor in the  tech industry is honestly just to ask  i think there are so many amazing smart  people who  would be more than happy to give advice  and to share their learnings and their  knowledge  find the person who's willing to bring  you into a really really tough  conversation  with a really really senior person  without any sort of preparation  but they trust you enough to handle your  own i think that's the type of person  that you might want to learn from  be very respectful of your mentor's time  once you have identified the person who  inspires you the most  who you would want to be then reach out  over email social media  with specific guidance on the exact  thing that you are looking to accomplish  i find that more details you provide  that makes it easier  for you to receive help find people you  admire  like people you're really inspired by  and do some research on the things they  have written on the internet so that  they don't have to re-explain the basics  since they probably already share these  things online  and after understanding what it is that  you want to learn from these folks  reach out to them for virtual coffee  if they're in your organization's  directory  if they are external reach out to them  via platforms like linkedin  and once you build a rapport keep  chatting with them once a quarter  the way to find good mentor in the tech  industry is to just being open  and approaching people that you admire  even if it's for just one small thing  and asking them if you can spend some  time  with them learning about it rather than  having one mentor that i go to for  questions across the board  i tend to seek out those i admire in  specific areas  so for example when i was looking at  moving careers i talked to a co-worker  that had actually made a really similar  move  and got advice from her on how to get  started  and in another situation when i was  really hesitating for this big  risky but good decision i talked to  another co-worker who i find  absolutely fearless and she definitely  helped talk me into it  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you

